  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-window-close sets https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#is-closing and proceeds with https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#definitely-close-a-top-level-traversable. That might return without actually closing the window if https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#checking-if-unloading-is-canceled and won't clear `#is-closing`.\n\nBoth Firefox and Chrome reproduce this bug, I didn't test Safari.\n- To get a script-closable window, open a new window from script: `window.open()`\n- In that script-closable window, set `onbeforeunload = () => false; document.body.innerHTML = '<iframe src=\"https://example.com\"></iframe><iframe></iframe>'`\n- From both iframe evaluation contexts, try `top.close(); console.log(top.closed)`. The cross process iframes will be left with `top.closed=true`.",
